# Inactive v2 marker transport — implementation notes

Source-only preparation for the next bounded batch on repository base `d69c985d865fd59f2cfcd64be08c2f5938eb81ba`. Read repository `AGENTS.md`, latest continuation block, lifetime-change contract, existing v2 capacity/proof transports and legacy capacity-marker semantics before implementing. New files only; no existing source, settings, dependency, runtime route or SQL was edited by this work unit.

## Contract

- `createVoiceV2MarkRpcPorts(client).mark(request)` invokes only `bfa_p5_v2_capacity_mark` with `{ p_request: request }`.
- Request has exactly `protocol: 2`, the complete twelve-field v2 proof with operation `inspect`, immutable canonical lowercase nonnil `operationId` UUID, and `expectedPoolVersion` safe integer from 1 through `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`.
- Ack has exactly `protocol: 2`, the complete exact original request, and status `marked | already-marked | denied | quarantined | closed`.
- Every immutable proof, claim, binding, original-time, operation-ID and expected-version field must match on all statuses. No coercion, added fields, accessors, hidden/symbol fields or inherited record authority is accepted. Null-prototype own-data records remain supported.
- Parsed snapshots are detached and all nested records frozen. The mandatory client method and receiver are captured once; one transport invocation per valid deliberate call. Failures expose only `voice-v2-mark-rpc-unavailable`, without a cause or raw details.
- No local clock, Auth verifier, SDK/client construction, credentials, provider, fallback, transparent retry or operation/proof-ID generation is installed. Hosts must independently establish genuine nonretrying transport and current Auth/service provenance.
- A separate fresh exact inspect proof is mandatory. An earlier capacity inspection consumes its own receipt. Shape validation does not establish unused status or freshness; SQL does.
- `marked` is a database observation only. `already-marked` cannot authorize repeating an external create. Failed/malformed replies may follow committed effects; preserve original identities and uncertain held accounting. Closed status does not establish whole-operation provider finality or a refund. Runtime orchestration and the quiesced no-fallback cutover remain deferred.

## Checks

First primary run: **90/90 passing**. First scoped ESLint: **passing**. Both diagnostic logs are preserved, with no overwritten failure log. Prettier formatted only the two new owned files before these checks. The Vitest run retains the existing `vite-tsconfig-paths` advisory; no configuration/dependency change was made.

