Snapshots compare 22 tables and filter only exact permitted target rows. The primary marker and terminal-lifecycle cases seed nonzero unrelated same-owner P3b/legacy held records, which remain byte-for-byte equal. No accounting tables, resets, new quota/debits/refunds, or old code/schema constraints changed. The actual marker survives terminal fencing and unchanged exact legacy close; a fictional unknown operation observation retains the marked slot, and fictional whole-operation not-created finality through unchanged reconciliation releases only occupied slot while held/debited units persist. Role assertions deny anon/authenticated public execution and all caller execution of private helpers or access to private shared tables.

Committed lost/malformed reply doubles retain marker/proof and do not retry; separate injected allocation-write SQL exception rolls back the whole transaction and preserves the entire snapshot. These distinguish post-COMMIT uncertainty from transaction rollback, without generalizing all errors into consumption or no-commit guarantees.

