## Smallest next meaningful dependency

Implement the missing isolated **v2 post-issuance current-eligibility reader and its strict inactive transport**, with actual SQL composition tests, before attempting the v2 verification/owned admission bridge. This is a concrete missing protected observation, not another generic wrapper or repeated planning batch.

The actual marker is embedded in `voice-store-adapter.server.ts`, not a separate marker file. That bridge currently constructs `createVoiceServerVerifier`, reads the expiring v1 session fence, and uses unversioned cleanup/proof registration and `{claim,state}` acknowledgment mappings. `voice-rpc-store.server.ts` also maps old capacity claim, base-only inspect and close. These cannot simply accept the new marker port or provide v2 orchestration.

The existing `bfa_p5_voice_read_current`/`voice-read-rpc.server.ts` snapshot includes current thread, generation, allowlist, issuance and exact attempt approval, but has no explicit protocol, actual Auth session/parent version or immutable v2 issuance binding. The completed v2 current-thread reader is intentionally pre-issuance and lacks issuance/approval; parent/issuance reads do not provide one atomic approval/current-thread observation. The v2 proof predicate already requires exact cleanup and a full approved claim, so it cannot supply the earlier verification observation needed to construct that claim.

The new reader should require the host's independently verified actual Auth owner/session and expected parent version, exact fingerprint, thread and attempt. Under shared owner-first locks it must reject any legacy fence, missing/revoked/version-changed parent or mismatched protocol-2 issuance binding, then return only exact current thread/generation/allowlist, bounded immutable issuance and matching unrevoked voice approval. The parent adds no time allowance. Preserve safe post-lock clock/high-water checks, issuance/approval/allowlist expiry, exact source timestamp/incarnation/revision and no private-content reads. Null remains denial without parent creation/revocation, legacy adoption, registration, accounting mutation or fallback. Define whether the reader leaves owner high-water unchanged explicitly, consistent with its intended observation contract; never describe a read as a lock spanning remote Auth or later admission.

After that real dependency is tested, the v2 verifier can use unchanged local unseal/HMAC against fresh request-bound Auth and this protected snapshot, producing exact content-free parent/fingerprint evidence with conservative time. A subsequent owned bridge can compose completed v2 cleanup/proof/capacity/mark transports while preserving one-attempt operation identity and exact legacy cleanup. Do not install a broad dispatcher or unused generic facade. Existing service lifecycle coordination and admission state machines require a focused provenance audit before integration; provider creation remains outside all these slices.

Original v5 remains complete; P4 approval/expiry null and grants empty; P3b accounts/staging closed with retained accounting. No paid Lovable edit, real Auth/model/voice/microphone call, connected SQL/settings change, activation, publication, AWS or billing action occurred. All 21 native cases and cross-backend/deployed Auth/provider/device acceptance remain unrun.

